# R3-05: the same explicit classification and facts support both teaching and card.
i=item('7.3',6)
i['prompt']='Describe these fictional education routes and give a reasoned judgement for a learner seeking recognised technical skills. Here, a community apprenticeship illustrates traditional education through local craft learning and daily participation; it provides no formal qualification. A reachable college course illustrates modern institutional education through technical theory and an assessed qualification, but charges affordable fees and reduces earning time. Both are feasible.'
i['canonical_answer']='Traditional community learning offers locally relevant practice without course fees, but in this case gives no formal qualification and may cover a narrower range of technical knowledge. Modern college education provides structured theory and an assessed qualification, but involves fees and less time for earning. College better fits the stated aim of recognised technical skills if its qualification is accepted and costs remain manageable. Community learning may better fit a different aim centred on local craft practice. Judge the stated routes rather than assume that all traditional or modern education has identical quality.'
i['marking_guidance']=['Description: identify the traditional/community and modern/institutional routes and their stated features.','Judgement: weigh practical relevance and recognition against fees and time for earning, using the learner’s stated aim.','Reason: develop a conditional conclusion; do not invent an allowance or recognised apprenticeship assessment.','Original indicative practice guidance; not an official mark scheme.']
block('7.3',2,'02')['text']='In a fictional comparison, a community apprenticeship teaches local craft through participation, illustrating traditional education; it offers no formal qualification. A college course illustrates modern institutional education with technical theory and an assessed qualification, alongside affordable fees and reduced earning time. Community learning can suit local practical aims. College better fits a learner seeking recognised technical skills if the qualification is accepted and its costs are manageable. These are features of the stated examples, not fixed properties of all traditional or modern education.'

# R3-06: assessment provenance belongs in claim evidence, not in learner prose.
sdg='The Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) combine economic, social and environmental pillars—livelihoods, well-being and natural systems—with ambitions for 2030. Examples are SDG 1, No Poverty; 2, Zero Hunger; 3, Good Health and Well-being; 4, Quality Education; 5, Gender Equality; 6, Clean Water and Sanitation; 8, Decent Work and Economic Growth; 12, Responsible Consumption and Production; and 13, Climate Action. Climate-related drought and flooding threaten crops, water and infrastructure, undermining livelihoods and development gains. Suitable adaptation reduces vulnerability, while reducing emissions limits further warming and protects future needs. A particular local event cannot be attributed to climate change merely because it occurred.'
block('1.2',1,'R01')['text']=sdg
sdgc=next(c for c in TOPICS['1.2']['ledger']['claims'] if c['claim_id']=='CLM-6136-1.2-01-00-90')
