# R3-07: one action, one reason and one goal within the existing three-mark slot.
i=item('1.2',6)
i['prompt']='Suggest one responsible-production response for a fictional tailoring group that discards usable fabric offcuts while buying new fabric for small bags. Explain one resource-saving benefit and name one Sustainable Development Goal directly supported by the action.'
i['canonical_answer']='Sort suitable offcuts and use them for the small bags. This reduces the new fabric required and the usable fabric discarded, provided the pieces fit the required bag sizes. It directly supports SDG 12, Responsible Consumption and Production.'
i['marking_guidance']=['Context, 1 mark: a feasible reuse response addressing the offcuts and small bags.','Reason, 1 mark: connect that response to reduced new-material use or avoidable waste; do not count the same benefit twice.','Goal, 1 mark: identify SDG 12 or its title, Responsible Consumption and Production. No paid-work assumption or second goal is required.','Original indicative practice guidance; not an official mark scheme.']

# R3-08: preserve the two-mark contrast and add three-pillar description through
# an existing three-mark applied performance subpart, retaining all slot labels.
i=item('2.2',3)
i['canonical_answer']='Economic advancement concerns productive opportunities and employment. Infrastructure development concerns supporting networks such as water, electricity and transport.'
i['marking_guidance']=['Comparison, up to 2 marks: distinguish productive opportunities/employment from supporting physical networks. Give credit for one accurate feature of each pillar, not two repetitions of the same feature.','Original indicative practice guidance; not an official mark scheme.']
i=item('2.2','P02')
i['prompt']='Describe (a) how three pillars of the first Harambee Prosperity Plan are illustrated by this fictional programme [3]: an audit team publishes spending decisions, apprentices gain productive skills for paid work, and maintained electricity connections serve workshops. Suggest (b) an immediate response where four training centres have opened but only one has regular tutors and attendance has not improved; qualified tutors can be reassigned within the available budget [3].'
i['canonical_answer']='(a) Effective governance is illustrated by published spending decisions that support accountability. Economic advancement is illustrated by skills for productive paid work. Infrastructure development is illustrated by maintained electricity networks serving workshops. (b) Reassign suitable tutors to the operating centres and publish a reliable timetable, checking their availability and the effect on other centres. This makes existing training space more usable instead of merely increasing building numbers. Monitor attendance and learning access to see whether the delivery barrier has improved.'
i['marking_guidance']=['Evidence (a), 3 marks: describe three distinct HPP pillars by linking each to its supplied action and contribution. A bare list of labels is insufficient; allow other accurate descriptions supported by the source.','Meaning (b), up to 3 marks: propose a feasible tutor/timetable response, connect it to usable training access and explain how delivery will be checked within the available resources.','Original indicative practice guidance; not an official mark scheme.']

# R3-09: recognition practice occupies an existing two-mark State subpart.
i=item('1.2','P01')
i['prompt']=i['prompt'].replace('what is meant by renewable and non-renewable resources','two pillars of sustainable development')
i['canonical_answer']='(a) Any two of the economic, social and environmental pillars. (b) Cutting 130 trees while only 90 regenerate gives a net loss of 40 trees annually. If the rates persist, the woodland stock declines despite the resource being renewable. That decline can reduce resources available for future users. Limiting extraction and protecting regeneration addresses this mechanism; the renewable label alone does not establish sustainable use.'
i['marking_guidance']=['Point (a), 2 marks: name any two distinct pillars from economic, social and environmental; one mark for each.','Development (b), up to 4 marks: compare extraction with regeneration, establish the declining stock, connect it to future needs and explain a matched response or condition. A definition without application is insufficient.','Original indicative practice guidance; not an official mark scheme.']
